Apply a scene's startup hold angles at load, before the first physics step.

Generated against unitree_mujoco ae6a8403e272733e9996ef59990880330496177f, on top of 001-008.

007 added `startup_hold_<joint>` equalities and hands each to its motor on the first tick, but the
joints still SPAWN at the URDF zero and the equality drags them to the held angle over the first
few steps. Since 008 gave the fingers contact geometry that drag is a hand sweeping through
whatever it spawned inside: in the tabletop world the right hand starts inside the green cylinder
and throws it across the room.

ApplyStartupPose writes the angle into qpos at load, so the equality is satisfied at t=0 and
nothing swings. Its own source is COPYed in by the Dockerfile from workspace/vendor and is NOT
part of this patch; this registers it in main.cc's three model-load paths and in the build.

